00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.980
But zooming in reveals they aren't holes at
all.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.830
It looks like they're not depressions but are
raised areas, mounds of some sort.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:13.130
When I look at the image, the idea that these
structures could be some type of burial

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.750
mounds is plausible.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:21.140
Giant burial mounds have been discovered
elsewhere in the Amazon dating back as far as

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.850
6000 years ago.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:29.230
If the satellite has revealed an undiscovered
ancient burial site, then its scale is

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.250
unparalleled.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.460
It's so vast.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.700
The possibility that they could be burial
mounds is amazing.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.700
Funk is skeptical of the burial mound theory.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.480
There's so many of them.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.600
You know, the burial mounds are usually
reserved for, you know, chiefs and high

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.010
priests and rich people.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.510
Yet what they are is hard to tell.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:57.540
There's nothing like this in the world that I
know of, and I've never heard anything about

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:57.960
them.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:06.140
The mounds sit in a 386,000 square mile
wilderness known as the White Forest.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:16.020
What we call cassinga, which is a dry land,
thorny deciduous vegetation that's really

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.620
totally intertwined.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:21.060
You can't see more than 20, 30ft in.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.340
Hey, this should be the spot.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:59.900
Led by the image coordinates Fudge treks West
seeking signs of the mounds among the thorns

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.710
